# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF (the runner image sets
# `core.autocrlf=true`), and `biome check` — which formats to LF — reports every
# file as mis-formatted, which is why the Windows lint leg had to be dropped.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets git's text heuristic does not always recognise: never convert them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.wasm binary

# Vendored sources are byte-for-byte copies of upstream trees; normalising them
# would create diffs against upstream for no benefit.
vendor/** -text
